//@version=6
// Order-type test strategy 7 — Long LIMIT below market, cancelled on a red candle
//
// Pure order-lifecycle test (NO fill expected): on a GREEN candle place a resting
// long-limit entry 5% under the prior close — far below market, so it should rest,
// not fill; on the next RED candle, cancel the pending order. Exercises the plugin's
// place-limit -> rest -> cancel path (a plain NORMAL LO on DNSE), not fills/brackets.
//
// 1 contract VN30F1M. The entry comment carries the SIGNAL price; the trade CSV's
// Price column carries the actual handling, so the two can be compared.

// VN30F1M notional = price x 100,000 VND/point (~192.5m at 1925), and DNSE's loan
// package quotes initialRate ~0.1848 -> ~35.6m margin per contract. initial_capital
// must clear that or every entry is rejected on margin.
strategy("T7 Long limit below, cancel on red", overlay=true, pyramiding=0,
     initial_capital=500000000, default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1,
     margin_long=18.48, margin_short=18.48,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=false)

isGreen = close > open
isRed   = close < open

// 5% under the PRIOR close. Far below market -> the limit should rest, not fill.
limitPrice = close[1] * 0.95

// GREEN candle: place / refresh the resting long-limit entry.
if isGreen
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, limit=limitPrice,
                   comment="E-lim@" + str.tostring(limitPrice, format.mintick))

// RED candle: cancel the pending limit order.
if isRed
    strategy.cancel("L")

// --- LAST PROTECTION LINE (live-test safe guard) ---
// Flatten everything if the open position is losing more than 0.1%. Price-based,
// so it is independent of the contract multiplier and fees. A fresh fill sits at
// ~0%, so this fires only on a real adverse move: open profit percent < -0.1.
PROTECT_PCT = -0.1

openPnlPct = strategy.position_size != 0 ? strategy.opentrades.profit_percent(strategy.opentrades - 1) : 0.0

if strategy.position_size != 0 and openPnlPct < PROTECT_PCT
    strategy.close_all(comment="PROTECT")

plot(strategy.position_size, "pos", display=display.data_window)
plot(limitPrice, "limit", display=display.data_window)
